 ### SCENARIO-PHASE4-067: Exp4261 Either Banks One New Level Or Stops With Decision-Grade No-Advance
 **Description:** Running Exp 4261 either writes `blocked_arc_fixtures_missing` when the offline solver import, survey, prior Exp 4249 evidence, or local fixture metadata cannot support the attempt, writes `complete: incremental_progress_no_advance_<game>_L<n>_<reason>` when the selected frontier has no verifier-validated real-env level increment in this bounded window, or writes `success: incremental_progress_<game>_advanced_to_L<n>_total20` only when the offline real environment confirms one new level after the margin-triggered verifier accepts the route. A successful run MUST set `total_levels=20`, `levels_completed=1`, `game_advanced` to the advanced game id, `real_env_confirmed=true`, `verifier_validated=true`, preserve model specs for the offline world-model solver and margin-triggered routing, and compute `reproducibility_checksum` from deterministic solver inputs and trajectory evidence. An honest no-advance run MUST keep `total_levels=19`, set `levels_completed=0`, set `game_advanced="none"`, set `real_env_confirmed=false`, keep the selected `target_game` and `target_level` attributable, and still satisfy the acceptance gate when `honest_verdict` is terminal-prefixed with `complete:`. A blocked run MUST keep `total_levels=19`, set `levels_completed=0`, set `game_advanced="none"`, and still satisfy the acceptance gate because the verdict is terminal-prefixed with `blocked_`.
+
+### REQ-PHASE4-068: ARC-AGI-3 Live Env Accuracy Probe Exp4262
+**Description:** The system SHALL run Exp 4262 as a scored-only live ARC-AGI-3 accuracy probe after Exp 4250 reached the live environment, beat the random floor on efficiency, and completed zero official `EnvironmentScore` levels. It MUST first check the official SDK import and live ARC endpoint before any online solver call, and if that live handshake cannot return a scorecard it MUST stop with `honest_verdict="blocked_arc_live_env_unreachable"`. It MUST statically preserve the Operator-Only External Publication rule by refusing any path that would close a scorecard or submit to a leaderboard, using `honest_verdict="blocked_operator_only_submission"` if no scored-only path exists. When reachable, it MUST target one best-headroom live game through the existing live adapter and margin-triggered solver routing, apply provenance-blind verifier routing metadata when the Exp 4256 hardened provenance-blind win survives, read only the open `EnvironmentScore`, and write `results/experiment_4262_arc_live_env_accuracy_probe.json` with bare top-level fields `honest_verdict`, `levels_completed`, `actions_vs_baseline_ratio`, `leaderboard_submitted`, `preconditions_checked`, `random_seed`, `reproducibility_checksum`, and `model_specs`. Those field principles MUST be exactly: `Terminal-prefixed. A level completion AND an honest 0-levels-efficiency-only are BOTH COMPLETE.`, `BARE int: real-env-confirmed levels (EnvironmentScore) -- the live accuracy metric; 0 is honest and decision-grade.`, `BARE float: actions taken / EnvironmentInfo.baseline_actions -- the efficiency metric (north-star §0 EFFICIENCY axis).`, `BARE bool=false -- confirms NO leaderboard submission (operator-only external publication).`, `Records live-env reachability + no-submit verified; pre-empts fabrication + the operator-only-submission violation.`, `Determinism precondition for the probe.`, `Hash of the probe config + trajectory; lets a third party re-run.`, and `The live-env adapter + verifier routing; required methodology.`.
+
+### SCENARIO-PHASE4-068: Exp4262 Reports Live Completion Metrics Or Blocks Honestly
+**Description:** Running Exp 4262 either writes `blocked_arc_live_env_unreachable` when the SDK import, ARC endpoint, or live scorecard handshake is unavailable, writes `blocked_operator_only_submission` when the only available live path would submit to a leaderboard, or writes a terminal-prefixed live artifact after the scored-only adapter fixture passes, the anonymous-key SDK enumerates the target environment, the margin-triggered solver executes under a bounded completion-sized action budget, and an open scorecard is read without leaderboard submission. A valid reachable artifact MUST set `levels_completed` to the bare integer from the official `EnvironmentScore`, set `actions_vs_baseline_ratio` to the bare float `actions_taken / baseline_actions`, set `leaderboard_submitted=false`, preserve `game_probed`, `actions_taken`, `baseline_actions`, `environment_score`, and `trajectory` evidence, include `preconditions_checked` with SDK reachability plus no-submit verification, declare `random_seed=4262`, compute `reproducibility_checksum` from the probe config and trajectory, include model specs for the live adapter, margin-triggered routing, and provenance-blind routing status, and pass the acceptance gate when those required fields are present with `leaderboard_submitted=false`, including the honest zero-level efficiency-only case.
